3. Use the `updateAAD` method to authenticate data:

```java
byte[] data = "your_data".getBytes();
byte[] tag = aead.updateAAD(data);
```

The `updateAAD` method takes the data to be authenticated as input and returns the authentication tag. You can then use this tag to verify the authenticity of the data.

4. To verify the authenticity of the data, use the `verifyAAD` method:

```java
byte[] data = "your_data".getBytes();
byte[] tag = aead.updateAAD(data);
boolean isAuthentic = aead.verifyAAD(tag, data);
```

The `verifyAAD` method takes the authentication tag and the data as input and returns a boolean value indicating whether the data is authentic or not.

Remember to replace `"your_secret_key"` and `"your_iv"` with your actual secret key and IV values.

