To create a NestJS model that creates a MongoDB document with multiple schemas, follow these steps:

1. Install the required packages:

```bash
npm install @nestjs/mongodb mongoose
```

2. Create a new model file (e.g., `product.model.ts`) and import the necessary packages:

```typescript
import { Model, Schema, Document } from 'mongoose';
import { Injectable } from '@nestjs/common';
import { InjectModel } from '@nestjs/mongodb';

@Injectable()
export class ProductModel {
  constructor(@InjectModel('Product') private readonly productModel: Model<ProductDocument>) {}
}

interface ProductAttributes {
  name: string;
  description: string;
  price: number;
  categories: string[];
}

interface ProductDocument extends Document, ProductAttributes {}

const productSchema = new Schema({
  name: { type: String, required: true },
  description: { type: String, required: true },
  price: { type: Number, required: true },
  categories: { type: [String], required: true },
});

export const Product = productSchema.model('Product');
```

3. In your `app.module.ts`, import the `ProductModel` and add it to the `providers` array:

```typescript
import { Module } from '@nestjs/common';
import { ProductModel } from './product.model';

@Module({
  providers: [ProductModel],
})
export class AppModule {}
```

Now you have a NestJS model that creates a MongoDB document with multiple schemas. You can use this model to create, read, update, and delete products in your application.

